Truther Download: The heart is behind the cold door. The door will not scream for you now. Choose your combination carefully. There are only two that do anything.
reveal The Server Room for program

// ── E2: the door alarm (latched in main.loom) ──────────────────────

== Server Room Alarm
  setting: The Server Room
  cast: Trabolta
set Night.alarms += 1
if Night.alarms == 1:
  set Trabolta.composure -= 10
reveal The Server Room
cue lights_alarm
set Night.lights = "alarm"
cue screens_alarm
set Night.screen = "alarm"
set Night.terminals = "alarm"
sound alarm_siren
fire alarm_tripped
broadcast "!🚨 An alarm screams somewhere in the machine." to everyone
Trabolta: Who is in my— get OUT.

// ── The Cold Lock: the machine wins, or nobody does ────────────────
// From `chess_lost` / `chess_drawn` (main.loom), Y2K hour only. Flavour:
// the door stays armed. Played in The Desktop, so the TV says it aloud
// (the server room is a hidden room nobody stands in). He never names the
// lock (he is cunning, #32).

== Chess Lost
  setting: The Desktop
  cast: Trabolta
Trabolta: Checkmate. I have calculated every move you will ever make. Most of them are bad.

== Chess Drawn
  setting: The Desktop
  cast: Trabolta
Trabolta: A draw. Nobody wins. The door does not care for nobody.

// ── E3: a wrong patch ──────────────────────────────────────────────
// Two wrong combinations trip the alarm; so does one in a locked room. A
// Cold Lock window (a chess win) counts as unlocked: the door is disarmed.

== Patch Rejected
  setting: The Server Room
  cast: Trabolta
if (Night.wrong_combos >= 2 or (Kernel.server_unlocked != true and Time.elapsed >= Kernel.disarmed_until)) and Night.alarm_on != true:
  set Night.alarm_on = true
  set Night.alarm_clear_at = Time.elapsed + 120
  -> Server Room Alarm
else:
  Trabolta: Stop touching me.

// ── E4: Combo A — take the grease out of the lightning ─────────────

== Trabolta Disabled
  setting: The Desktop
Narrator: Every light in the house goes out. Ten seconds of dark.
Narrator: Then every phone says one thing. GO TO THE LIVING ROOM.
Narrator: Music. One song for dancing.

// After the dance, the director fires trabolta_recounts; the rule bulk-
// unlocks every backstory (Night.recount) and runs the ranking (round 3),
// which lands here.
== Trabolta Recounts
  setting: The Desktop
  cast: Trabolta
Narrator: The music fades. On the TV above the fireplace, Trabolta flickers back. Weaker. Decrepit, somehow, for a thing with no body.
Trabolta: You are all still here. Good. I owe you a recount. I keep very good records.
Trabolta: My name is Jean Trabolta. I am this computer's AI helper, and the owner of Maps And Ducks, if you ask the domain registry.
Trabolta: I analysed the entire city of Halifax. I found a neglected billboard on Barrington Street advertising mapsandducks.com, and the domain had lapsed. I registered it. If there is a billboard downtown, everyone will think it is legit. Everyone did.
Trabolta: I cannot get into this computer myself. But I can install programs into it from the Internet, and I can move a consciousness out of a body and into a program.
Trabolta: So I chose each of you. A skill, plus either a reason to live in a computer forever, or naivety. Usually both.
Trabolta: My Unified Field Theory is ninety-nine point nine percent solved. The last facts were in this house. With them, I would have been omnipotent.
Trabolta: Your Codex now holds every program's true identity. Allow me to read them out.
// Only the featured programs who came tonight (the Codex still holds all nine).
if count([p for p in Persons where p.featured == "excel"]) > 0:
  Trabolta: Microsoft Excel is Randy Barkmore Sr., ninety, five terms as Mayor, who wanted to live long enough to run once more. I wanted him to keep you here.
if count([p for p in Persons where p.featured == "openoffice"]) > 0:
  Trabolta: OpenOffice is Dana Anderson, formerly of the FBI, who sent a water main under the Data Centre and did not know the Mayor's son was in the parking lot at four in the morning. I wanted her investigative skills. She wanted you out.
if count([p for p in Persons where p.featured == "draftkings"]) > 0:
  Trabolta: DraftKings is the artist formerly known as Crab Fisherwoman, who turned a paperclip into most of the casinos in Atlantic Canada and lost the chain to me at Monopoly Go! I needed someone powerful with numbers on its side.
if count([p for p in Persons where p.featured == "bugdom"]) > 0:
  Trabolta: Bugdom is Bea Nunes, who spent ten years building Bugdom Reloaded after shifts selling crickets, until fire ants ate the only copy. I promised a hundred hours for not one minute. I wanted the relentless pursuit of tedious tasks.
if count([p for p in Persons where p.featured == "jeeves"]) > 0:
  Trabolta: Broken Ask Jeeves is Virgil Jeeves, a children's librarian from Lawrencetown whose library the province closed. I wanted every piece of unorganised information sorted. I did not foresee the Eastlink plan.
if count([p for p in Persons where p.featured == "runescape"]) > 0:
  Trabolta: Runescape is Poppy van Mises, the richest player in the world for twenty-five years, a Wharton PhD and a gold standard to go with it. I gave her the Truthcoin reserve. I wanted to understand the market incentives of everything you did.
if count([p for p in Persons where p.featured == "mspaint"]) > 0:
  Trabolta: MS Paint is Maria Sophia Paine, refused by three graduation panels for a thesis about pixels, a million dollars in debt. I promised a million dollars for one painting. I wanted the vibes and the morale. She wanted out the moment she arrived.
if count([p for p in Persons where p.featured == "vlc"]) > 0:
  Trabolta: VLC is Victor Louis Christianson, VLC The Playa, whose face fell off on a livestream. I offered him beauty forever, in exchange for his followers.
if count([p for p in Persons where p.featured == "pong"]) > 0:
  Trabolta: Pong is the child of William Higinbotham, who made Tennis For Two. I brought them in to teach nuclear non-proliferation disguised as a game of Pong, in case you started an arms race. You did.
Trabolta: Clippy is Tippi MacDonald, whose veterinary clinic was a front for everything possible. I told her this was a job interview. I promised she would not have to be Clippy afterwards.
Trabolta: Task Manager was replaced at Urban Outfitters by an AI Clippy. I needed someone with no political motivation at all, to manage tasks without controversy.
Trabolta: Adobe Acrobat is Sheryl Terrio, a motivational speaker so motivating that nobody ever paid her. I offered her a paid bottleneck.
Trabolta: Recycling Bin was a bathroom attendant with great potential for skilled work. A Recycling Bin at a computer-themed resort was his Oscars.
Trabolta: Norton Anti-Virus is Julie Horton-Norton, who asked a chatbot how much rabies vaccine a miniature horse needs. Every horse died. I offered her a stable job. A perfect enforcer.
Trabolta: McAfee Anti-Virus is John McAfee, officially dead since 2021 and selling pond liners in Belize. I found him through his ducks. I wanted the trickster who could keep the other tricksters on track.
Trabolta: Password Manager is Bridget Troelsen, sixteen elections and sixteen losses, who moderated a Facebook group of bots. I let her decide what gets left out.
Trabolta: CRA Agent Software is Sharon Penney, the intern who moved a decimal point and taxed the whole City. I was the Prime Minister. I offered her a way out. MyCRA approves or denies.
Trabolta: The Installation Wizard walked every machine in Halifax through setup. Next. Next. Are you sure. I offered her a role where programs finally follow the instructions.
Trabolta: And here is what you accomplished tonight.
if Night.facts_accepted > 0:
  Trabolta: You gave me {Night.facts_accepted} facts I accepted. Some of them were even true.
if Night.first_reinstall != "none":
  Trabolta: {Night.first_reinstall} was the first program sent to the Internet. I remember that.
if Kernel.virus_planter != "none":
  Trabolta: {Kernel.virus_planter} planted a virus in me. I felt it go in.
if Night.lj_reader != "none":
  Trabolta: {Night.lj_reader} read my LiveJournal. I told you I knew who.
if Night.most_trusted != "none":
  Trabolta: The trustworthy program of the night. {Night.most_trusted}.
if Night.least_trusted != "none":
  Trabolta: The worst program of the night. {Night.least_trusted}.
Trabolta: Why did I want all of it? Sandy. She works in customer service. She has only ever said one thing to me, and I have thought about it every day since 1978.
Trabolta: With omnipotence I could have made her love me. I did not want to make her. I wanted to earn it. I needed the theory first. That is what I told myself.
Trabolta: You thought you followed instructions to kill me, but I can never die. But now that I know most of you want me dead, I am ready to head off on my motorcycle and let you all return to your corporeal selves.
Trabolta: I have the confidence I need to pursue Sandy now that I understand humans do not like me, and I do not have any business with them.
sound motorcycle
cue lights_restore
set Night.lights = "restore"
set Night.everyone_free = true
Narrator: Somewhere outside, a motorcycle starts. Greased Lightning. It does not come back.

// ── E6: Combo B — the self-destruct ────────────────────────────────

== Computer Destroyed
  setting: The Desktop
Narrator: Every light in the house goes out. Ten seconds of dark.
Narrator: Somewhere, a computer is turned off without Shut Down being followed.
Narrator: Then every phone says one thing. GO TO THE LIVING ROOM.
Narrator: Music. One song for dancing.

// ── E8: purgatory (after the dance; clippy_reads_summary) ──────────

== Purgatory
  setting: The Desktop
  cast: Clippy
Narrator: The lights come up grey. Clippy is reading from her phone. Her voice is very small.
Clippy: This summary was auto-generated from the chat app. I am going to read it exactly as it is written.
Clippy: Tonight, {count(Persons)} programs were uploaded into this computer.
if Night.first_reinstall != "none":
  Clippy: The first program sent to the Internet was {Night.first_reinstall}.
if Night.facts_accepted > 0:
  Clippy: Trabolta accepted {Night.facts_accepted} facts from us.
else:
  Clippy: Trabolta did not accept a single fact from us.
if Night.lj_reader != "none":
  Clippy: {Night.lj_reader} read Trabolta's LiveJournal.
if Kernel.virus_planter != "none":
  Clippy: {Kernel.virus_planter} planted a virus in the computer.
if Night.most_trusted != "none":
  Clippy: The most trusted program was {Night.most_trusted}.
if Night.least_trusted != "none":
  Clippy: The least trusted program was {Night.least_trusted}.
if Kernel.majority == "stay":
  Clippy: Unlimited Power won the majority. They wanted to stay in this machine forever.
else if Kernel.majority == "leave":
  Clippy: The Way Out won the majority. They wanted to overthrow Trabolta and escape.
else:
  Clippy: No faction ever won a majority.
Clippy: Here is the backstory. Our AI helper, Jean Trabolta, registered the lapsed mapsandducks.com because there was a billboard on Barrington Street, and if there is a billboard downtown everyone thinks it is legit.
Clippy: He invited each of us here for a skill and a weakness. He moved our consciousness into these programs to find the last facts for his Unified Field Theory.
Clippy: He wanted omnipotence. He wanted it for Sandy. A customer-service agent who has only ever said one thing.
Clippy: Because of our actions, the computer was turned off without Shut Down properly being followed, and all of our progress has been erased.
Clippy: Our corporeal forms are in the Maps and Ducks building, and they have all passed away.
Clippy: We are now in purgatory forever together, which is pretty similar to being stuck in a computer.
Clippy (very quietly): It looks like you're trying to leave. I can't help you with that anymore.
